# mm.audio

A portable audio interface. It is the two ends of an audio link and nothing
more: input, which captures a microphone's samples, and output, which plays a
codec's. Mixing, effects, resampling, and level policy are above this module;
the controller registers and the serial link are detail below it.

The link's two ends are separate because they are separate devices. A microphone
is an input a caller captures from; a codec is an output a caller plays to. Each
has its own initialize, its own description, and its own shutdown, so a board
that has one but not the other still composes, and a caller that wants both
names them.

The serial link the drivers ride on, and the buses a codec is programmed over,
are mm.mcu facilities. The drivers own those; a provider supplies the wiring.

The platform-interface marker makes a selected board's audio provider part of an
executable only when its ordinary closure reaches mm.audio.
